although much of the canon information  about the mandalorian jedi war is still  up in the air here's what we know so far  this is the history of the mandalorian  jedi war explained  as odd as it sounds the war started  because the mandalorians did not  understand the jedi when they first  encountered them  even at the end of the mandalorian  season 1 the armorer describes the jedi  as  an order of sorcerers due to this lack  of understanding the mandalorians  created weapons and armor  to better combat these mysterious new  opponents in 2017 comicbook.com  interviewed dave filoni about how the  star wars rebels episode  trials of the darksaber referenced the  mandalorian jedi war  he explained the mandalorian jedi war  that i have in my mind  is very much derived from the oldest  style of thinking of mandalorians  which was that their weapons their  arsenal their technology  had a massive increase once they  collided with the jedi  and found these force-wielding people  that had abilities they  didn't understand more and more  animosity occurred between the  mandalorians and jedi  once the latter group started  interfering with the former's crusades  the 2016 reference book star wars aliens  of the galaxy  details how a group of sword-wielding  mandalorians  known as the mandalorian crusaders  carried out a series of conquests  across the galaxy while in the inner rim  the crusaders devastated a planet called  abdurya out of contempt for the native  obdurians  who they viewed as dishonorable cowards  the mandalorian crusaders also fought  the jedi at some point during these  missions  murals of the mandalorian crusaders  fighting the jedi  were created and can be seen in a few  episodes of star wars the clone wars  as well as one episode of star wars  rebels  even though mandalorians and jedi were  at one point sworn  enemies a member of the former group did  create a lightsaber of his own  that member was tar vizla the first  mandalorian  ever inducted into the jedi order tara  created a unique  black colored lightsaber called the  darksaber during his time as a jedi  after he died the jedi kept the saber in  the jedi temple  but during the fall of the old republic  members of house vizsla  raided that temple and reclaimed the  sabre they used it to unite their people  and defeat anyone who opposed them  including jedi the darksaber would  become a symbol of power to the  mandalorians  and was used to unite them before and  after the mandalorian jedi war  the mandalorian jedi war became so  heated that near the end of their wars  the mandalorians turned concordia the  moon of their homeworld  into a mining base although the  mandalorians put up a good fight against  the jedi  it was not enough to save their  homeworld the mandalorian jedi war  ended with a final battle which caused a  cataclysm that scorched  much of mandalore into a white  uninhabitable wasteland  the jedi won the war but not all was  lost for the mandalorians as they  created hermetically sealed domed cities  on mandalore's surface  years after the mandalorian jedi war  ended many mandalorians  including satin crees did not want to  continue the cycle of violence that  almost destroyed their planet  they formed a peaceful movement called  the new mandalorians  42 years before the battle of yavin a  civil war broke out between the new  mandalorians  and the martial traditionalists who both  sought control for mandalore  the death toll during this war was a  primary reason why sateen became a  pacifist for the rest of her life  as duchess satine rebuilt mandalore and  it  thrived under her leadership for 20  years  mandalore went on to become an active  participant in the senate of the  galactic republic while still remaining  neutral throughout the majority of the  clone wars  of course many mandalorians still  opposed the new mandalorians pacifist  ideals and  wanted to return mandalore to its  warrior ways  these same mandalorians would go on to  form the terrorist organization  deathwatch under the leadership of  governor prix vizsla and sateen's sister  bocaton crees  deathwatch was initially aligned with  count dooku and the separatists  but they parted ways and eventually  joined forces with a renegade sith lord  named maul to take over mandalore  together maul  and vizsla devised a plan to make the  new mandalorians look  weak in order to gain the people's trust  death watch is here to save you from  these intergalactic gangsters that  threaten our great city  the plan was successfully carried out  and vizsla declared himself  ruler of mandalore but he betrayed maul  and imprisoned him  it didn't take long for maul to escape  which allowed maul to challenge vizsla  to a duel which he won  after beheading vizsla with the  darksaber maul declared himself the new  leader of death watch and installed a  puppet prime minister  while he ruled from the shadows after  becoming ruler of mandalore  maul retained the loyalty of most of the  members of death watch  but some members such as bo katan could  not accept the idea of an outsider  ruling mandalore  and led a resistance against him in the  seventh season of the clone wars  maul's reign is cut short after former  jedi knight ahsoka tano and bocaton  team up to launch a full-scale assault  in an attempt to liberate mandalore from  the clutches of the shadow collective  before ordering the other shadow  collective leaders to go into hiding  maul is captured but subsequently  escapes custody in the wake of order 66  the 2018 spin-off film solo a star wars  story  set after the events of the clone wars  season seven  reveals that maul established another  crime syndicate  called the crimson dawn even though  bogatan and her forces defeated maul and  freed mandalore from the shadow  collective  it didn't take long for the empire to  undo all that progress  after bogota refuses to comply with the  imperial occupation of her homeworld  clan saxon betrayed her and swore  allegiance to emperor palpatine  fortunately bo katan joined forces with  clan wren the mandalorian protectors  and members of the rebel alliance to  fight back against clan saxon  following this victory bocaton was given  the darksaber and took up the title of  manned allure  a title assumed by the sole leader of  the mandalorian people  unfortunately the empire would strike  back against the remaining mandalorians  in the form of the great  purge this event saw the deaths of many  mandalorians across the galaxy  and the empire stealing massive amounts  of vesgar  a metal alloy that mandalorians use to  create their  signature armor in the season one finale  of the mandalorian the tribe's armorer  tells dinjaran that he needs to reunite  the child with his people that mission  sends bando on a series of adventures  including one that puts him in direct  contact with bogatan and her fellow  mandalorian separatists  although they don't share jaron's rigid  adherence to the mandalorian creed  bokuton  ultimately helps him on his mission in  exchange for his help in raiding an  imperial ship  mando is initially led to believe the  separatists are simply trying to steal  weapons from the shattered empire but  it eventually becomes clear that boca  ton is really after the dark saber  now wielded by moff gideon living up to  her end of the deal  she also tells jaren where to find a  jedi telling him to seek out ahsoka tano  mando heads to the planet corvus a  deforested wasteland where sokatano has  been waging a war against the brutal  reign of a figure known as the  magistrate  upon mando's arrival he's shepherded to  an audience with the magistrate who  offers him a staff  made of pure baskar in exchange for  murdering  ahsoka instead he joins forces with  ahsoka  following a brief skirmish when they  meet in the corvus wastelands  mando offers to help ahsoka defeat the  magistrate in exchange for her accepting  and training the child  as expected the magistrate is no match  for the duo but  ahsoka is unable to live up to her end  of the deal  telling mando that she can't train the  child she's able to speak with him via  the force  and learns that his real name is grogu  and that he was trained on coruscant  before being taken during the fall of  the jedi  but she also discovers a great deal of  fear anger and  darkness in him and having been close to  anakin skywalker  she's all too aware of how those  feelings can be exploited  although ahsoka is unable or unwilling  to train grogu  she offers manda one other way to  fulfill his obligation  take him to the planet tython where  grogu may be able to tap into the force  at the site of some ancient temple ruins  and establish a connection with another  jedi  in the middle of that process however  grogu is kidnapped by moff gideon's  forces  mando gathers the crew to overtake  gideon's leg cruiser  and save the child after reaching  groku's cell mando battles gideon  ultimately mando disarms gideon with the  best guard spear he received from ahsoka  back on corvus after taking grogu and a  shackled gideon to the bridge  mando offers the darksaber to bogatan  but she refuses  gideon clarifies that the darksaber  cannot be given  and must be won in combat their standoff  is interrupted when a jedi  luke skywalker himself arrives to rescue  them from a squad of dark troopers  and take grogo away to be trained will  mando and grogu's connection last  or will the events of the mandalorian  jedi war repeat themselves once again  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite star wars histories are  coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]

